<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uzziah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uzziah, also called Azariah, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> for much of the 8th century BCE. The Bible credits him with defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philistines">Philistines</a>, rebuilding Elath on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>, fortifying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and reorganising the army, and archaeology shows a time of growing settlement and prosperity. He was struck by leprosy late in life, and his son Jotham governed as regent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uzziah.jpg" alt="Uzziah" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume Rouille · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ozias-Uzziah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
